Tailwind CSS- 
What is Tailwind CSS?
Professional Definition
Tailwind CSS is a utility-first, open-source CSS framework that provides low-level utility classes to build modern, responsive, and customizable user interfaces directly within HTML without writing traditional custom CSS for every component.
Tailwind CSS was created by Adam Wathan, a Canadian web developer and educator.
0r
A utility-first CSS framework packed with classes like flex, pt-4, text-center, and rotate-90 that can be composed to build any design, directly in your markup."


